.TH "PB-CONFIG-REPOSITORY-CREDENTIALS-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-repository-credentials-set - Read a credential profile from a private JSON file or stdin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config repository credentials set <repository> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a credential profile from a private JSON file or stdin

.PP
Resolve a custom Git repository by ID or name and read its authentication profile from --file. Use --file - for stdin. The profile is validated and stored privately on this machine for repository access.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--file\fP=""
	private profile file; use - for stdin

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-repository-credentials(1)\fP
